# Cornell Box test fixture — license + provenance

## Project's adopted license

This fixture is distributed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
Unported (CC BY 3.0) License** — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

Attribution chain:
  - Original physical Cornell Box + matching virtual geometry:
      Donald Greenberg and students at Cornell University, 1984.
      http://www.graphics.cornell.edu/online/box/data.html
  - OBJ + MTL files (CornellBox-Original.obj + CornellBox-Original.mtl):
      Guedis Cardenas and Morgan McGuire at Williams College, 2011.
      https://casual-effects.com/data/
      Historical canonical URL: http://graphics.cs.williams.edu/data
  - Vendored into objtomc on 2026-07-04 (Session 30; this commit).

## Upstream license claims (verbatim)

The upstream archive at the awesome-3d-meshes mirror
(https://github.com/jvm-graphics-labs/awesome-3d-meshes/blob/master/McGuire/Cornell%20Box/CornellBox.zip)
contains TWO contradictory license statements. Both are reproduced
verbatim below.

### Claim 1: collection-level copyright.txt (inside CornellBox.zip)

The following is the verbatim content of `copyright.txt` from inside
the zip archive distributed by Morgan McGuire's Computer Graphics
Archive. It applies to the COLLECTION of 8 OBJ files:

    # A set of eight Cornell Boxes in OBJ format.
    # Note that the real box is not a perfect cube, so
    # the faces are imperfect in this data set.
    #
    # Created by Guedis Cardenas and Morgan McGuire at Williams College, 2011
    # Attribution 3.0 Unported (CC BY 3.0) License
    # http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
    #
    # http://graphics.cs.williams.edu/data

### Claim 2: per-file Public Domain header (in CornellBox-Original.obj + .mtl)

The following is the verbatim file-header comment block from both
CornellBox-Original.obj and CornellBox-Original.mtl. It applies to
the specific variant (Original) we have vendored:

    # The original Cornell Box in OBJ format.
    # Note that the real box is not a perfect cube, so
    # the faces are imperfect in this data set.
    #
    # Created by Guedis Cardenas and Morgan McGuire at Williams College, 2011
    # Released into the Public Domain.
    #
    # http://graphics.cs.williams.edu/data
    # http://www.graphics.cornell.edu/online/box/data.html

### Claim 3: awesome-3d-meshes catalog README

The awesome-3d-meshes mirror's catalog README
(https://github.com/jvm-graphics-labs/awesome-3d-meshes/blob/master/McGuire/Cornell%20Box/README.md)
declares:

    License: CC BY 3.0
    © 2009 Morgan McGuire

## Resolution

The per-file `.obj` and `.mtl` headers say "Released into the Public
Domain"; the collection `copyright.txt` and the catalog README say
"CC BY 3.0". This is a real discrepancy that we have resolved
conservatively in favor of the stricter CC BY 3.0 reading.

Rationale (per `research/cornell_box_tier4_proposal.md` §1.5 +
`DECISIONS.md` 2026-07-03 "Cornell Box multi-material Tier-4 scope
(v0.2 work item #1)"):

  1. Honoring attribution satisfies BOTH readings — Public Domain
     doesn't forbid attribution; CC BY 3.0 requires it. The strict
     reading subsumes the permissive reading.
  2. Attribution is good practice regardless. The Williams College
     Cornell Box variants are the de-facto standard test scene in
     computer graphics; ignoring the attribution requirement to
     claim Public Domain would be both legally aggressive and
     socially uncollegial toward Morgan McGuire and Guedis Cardenas.
  3. Matches the project's established vendoring pattern
     (DECISIONS.md 2026-06-18 "Vendoring pattern for third-party
     C++ deps" + DECISIONS.md 2026-06-18 "Stanford bunny test fixture
     provenance"): each vendored upstream gets a LICENSE record with
     verbatim upstream-license text + attribution + re-derivation
     provenance.

Anyone redistributing these files (in source or compiled form) must
preserve the CC BY 3.0 attribution. The full CC BY 3.0 license text
is at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/legalcode.

